    <h2>A race to the bottom, run through the courts</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      Competitive federalism assumes rivalry corrects itself. Here it did the opposite: courts came to be judged by their
      usefulness to the state’s economy rather than their independence, and the costs fell on people without market power.
    </p>

